<!--
  Every size is listed, and that is the point: QIcon picks the nearest entry
  rather than scaling one image, so the 16px cut — which is drawn rather than
  resampled — is what a tab strip actually gets.
-->
<RCC>
  <!-- `/icon`, matching the directory and what `main.cpp` asks for.

       It was `/icons` while main.cpp said `:/icon/`, so every addFile found
       nothing and the application had no icon at all. The rename to singular
       directory names changed the C++ path and left this prefix behind, and
       QIcon::addFile reports a missing resource by returning quietly.

       Deliberately not `/icons`, which is Qt's conventional place for an icon
       *theme* inside resources. These are the app's own marks rather than a
       theme, and the two should not share a path.

       (No double hyphens in here: XML forbids them inside a comment, and rcc
       refuses the file with a parse error that names a column rather than the
       reason.) -->
  <qresource prefix="/icon">
    <file>hydra-16.png</file>
    <file>hydra-24.png</file>
    <file>hydra-32.png</file>
    <file>hydra-48.png</file>
    <file>hydra-64.png</file>
    <file>hydra-128.png</file>
    <file>hydra-256.png</file>
  </qresource>
  <!-- The toolbar's own icons, and the reason they exist is uniformity.

       Every one of these was previously asked of the host icon theme, with a
       Qt standard pixmap behind it. That gives a different toolbar on every
       machine, and on some machines no toolbar icon at all: the shield fell
       back to SP_VistaShield, which is a Windows standard pixmap and comes
       back empty on Linux styles, and the key fell back to SP_CustomBase,
       which is explicitly a null icon. Reported as "we have no shield icons
       here", which is exactly what that produces.

       A separate prefix from /icon, which holds the application's own marks
       at fixed sizes. These are interface furniture and scale, so they are
       svg. Deliberately not /icons, which is Qt's conventional place for an
       icon THEME inside resources; this is not a theme and should not be
       mistaken for one by anything that goes looking. -->
  <qresource prefix="/ui">
    <file alias="back.svg">ui/back.svg</file>
    <file alias="forward.svg">ui/forward.svg</file>
    <file alias="reload.svg">ui/reload.svg</file>
    <file alias="stop.svg">ui/stop.svg</file>
    <file alias="drawer.svg">ui/drawer.svg</file>
    <file alias="media.svg">ui/media.svg</file>
    <file alias="key.svg">ui/key.svg</file>
    <file alias="shield.svg">ui/shield.svg</file>
    <file alias="annoyed.svg">ui/annoyed.svg</file>
    <file alias="confirm.svg">ui/confirm.svg</file>
  </qresource>
</RCC>
